From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Aug 30 15:10:11 2001
From: Kevin Dea <kdea () alpine-la ! com>
Date: Thu, 30 Aug 2001 15:10:11 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: huge (16-24 GB) ramdisk?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653669622208


Hello Managers,

Because we are dealing with extremely large files and our computational
work is I/O heavy, one of our software managers thought it would be a
good idea to create a large ramdisk or memory file system, in the order
of 16-24GB (yes, Gigabytes).  We certainly have enough memory on the
ES40 to accomodate the request.  I've scan through what I could on the
tru64 archives and I haven't noticed anyone trying anything on this
large a scale.  Most are a few tens of MB and perhaps the largest I've
seen attempted was 2GB.  

The entry on the /etc/fstab would be:

-s32768000		/ramdisk	mfs rw 1 0 

