Halted system, tried cp, got "read only file system",
then ran bcheckrc, that mounted root, and I copied it
back. 



Thanks to all who sent in their suggestions.
Couldn't locate cd!! .....single user worked!
Those are the gotcha's of using sudo!! when u make a
mistake, there is no going back.
Like in this case, if I had root shell, I would simply
copy it back as many suggested. 
For those unaware of sudo, once one is in the file
sudoers, he can execute commands as root, by doing 
sudo <command>  (it checks ur auth. everytime), so
after moving passwd passwd.old, it couldn't validate
me. This is a nice way to make sure all commands
executed as root as logged, by user name.


*********************************         
