From tru64-unix-managers  Mon Aug 27 17:11:35 2001
From: Wade Buchanan <Wade.Buchanan () wcom ! com>
Date: Mon, 27 Aug 2001 17:11:35 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: chk_bf_quota: group quota underflow
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653669622119

Thanks to everyone who replied on the quota issue:

Dela Acolatse, Bryan Lavelle, John Venier, Robert Bumpus, Derk Tegeler, Jeff
Spence.

The general consensus is that this is a known, and common error that is
harmless and can be ignored.  It sounds as if Compaq is also aware of the
issue as well.  However I did get a couple of responses that explained
possibly how to get rid of this error.  See Below:

Bryan Lavelle said:
This message is just an irritant, doesn't reflect a problem.  You MAY be
able to get rid of it by properly using user and group quotas, i.e. build
quota option into kernel, turn quotas on in rc.config, add userquota and
groupquota options to all advfs filesystems in your fstab and then run
quotacheck -a.  I've seen it fix the message and not fix it as well.

Jeff Spence said:
By design AdvFS checks for quota inconsistency.

To address the problem: set up quotas, run quotacheck, and then quotaoff.

1.  Set the QUOTA option in /sys/conf/HOSTNAME.  Rebuild kernel if required.
2.  Using rcmgr, set quota option to yes.
    #/usr/sbin/rcmgr set QUOTA_CONFIG yes
3.  Edit /etc/fstab, add quotatas to the fileset so it is mounted with
quotas.  This should be done even if you are NOT using quotas
    (dmn_users#users   /usr/users   advfs  rw,userquota,groupquota 0 2)
4.  umount and mount the fileset to enable change
5.  #quotacheck -v /usr/users (or whatever the fileset is)

Then quotas can be toggles off/on usong quotaoff/quotaon

Wade Buchanan
S4 Unix Systems Administrator
Worldcom



