defaults only allow for 128 pages, or 50,000 files=2E  Read the man page=20=
for more info and look at the '-x' and '-p' options=2E  You can't change=20=
this on the fly, but we were fortunate to have two identical raid sets,=20=
one of which hasn't been implemented yet=2E  If you feel like checking your=20=
BMT allocation to check you're not getting close to the limit use the=20=
command,

/sbin/advfs/vbmtpg /dev/rzc40c | pg

PAGE LBN    32 megaVersion   3 nextFreePg   0 freeMcellCnt  21 pageId=20=
   0

The top line shows 'freeMcellCnt' as 21, this is good=2E  Previously ours=20=
said 0=2E  This is bad!

Appparently this works differently in 5=2Ex and above=2E This is handled=20=
automatically, but domains need to be recreated after an upgrade, it=20=
doesn't happen automatically=2E

