Noone replied. I got into contact with compaq support.
The problem was the attached SCSI hardware. The "EasyRaidII" IDE to scsi
raid system does not respond to some scsi iniq commands and hence
generation of a wwid fails. I have tried several ways to work around by
editing /etc/ddr.dbase. This was what compaq suggested (but did not work):
# SCSIDEVICE
#     #
#     Type = disk
#     Name = "easyRAID"
#     #
#     ATTRIBUTE:
#         AttributeName = "VPDinfo"
#         Length = 16
#         ubyte[1] = 1
#         ubyte[5] = 15
Yes. it is commented out...(now)

I found that the problem was more in hardware. Infact the easy raid did
not respond to the "show inq pages supported" command. A firmware update
solved the problem. Now the array responds to the command like this:
scu> show inq pages supported

Vital Product Data Pages Supported by Device /dev/rdisk/dsk26c (II):

            Supported Vital Product Data Page (Code = 0x00)
                      Unit Serial Number Page (Code = 0x80)
                   Device Identification Page (Code = 0x83)
                         Vendor Specific Page (Code = 0xc0)

and it works. Same special device on all cluster nodes. 

Strange though that even with the old faulty firmware hwmgr -show scsi
-did X -f gave the same wwid on both nodes and a "valid" state, but
different special devices.....


regards,
--Armin

