To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: v5.1 and OpenSSH 2.9p2 login problems
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653669622032

Well, I knew it was something silly simple, and I'd like to thank

Stu Fuess <fuess@***.***.***>
Paul A Sand <pas@***.***.***>

for pointing out what the issues were.

1) The data structure for utmp/wtmp/finger/etc was changed between
    Digital UNIX 4 and Tru64 UNIX 5.  Which probably explains why both
    files were deleted and started fresh after my upgrades from 4.0D to
    5.1.

2) I had a lingering copy of sshd from ssh 1.2.26 still in /usr/sbin/.

So after deleting that copy and deleting both utmp and wtmp for good
measure, all symptoms disappeared.  Yay!

A link provided by Stu Fuess:

http://www.ornl.gov/its/archives/mailing-lists/tru64-unix-managers/1999/09/msg00183.html

originally I asked:
>Recently upgraded Digital Personal Workstation 433au from Digital
>UNIX 4.0D to Tru64 UNIX 5.1 (yes, went thru 5.0 and 5.0A).  Installed
>OpenSSL 0.9.6b, compiled with gcc.  OpenSSH 2.9p2 seems to compile
>fine and install fine, replacing previously installed (under 4.0D
>ssh 1.2.26).  However, the trouble starts when a user logs
>in remotely via ssh.
>
>Under 'finger', none of the user login information is correct.  They
>are listed as Dec 31st at 16:00, and from where they are logged in
>is not listed.  The last command lists them as being still logged in
>even after they log out.  "w" doesn't list a tty and their login time
>is again listed as Dec 31st at 16:00.
