was called in to analyze the network. 

After analysis it was determined that the GS140 was
retransmitting TCP packets at 323 millisecond
intervals. 

The kernel parameters are set as follows:

tcp_rexmit_interval_min   2
tcp_rexmit_max   128

How can it be possible that the Alpha is
retransmitting packets at 323 ms when the minimum rate
is set to "2" (which I believe is 1 second)..?

