Content-Type: text/plain;
	charset="iso-8859-1"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

I figured out what the problem was.  The /usr/ucb/lpr file had the wrong =
file permissions.  The Word Perfect site indicated the permission should =
be set to 6711, but doing this it disables all the users printing =
capabilities.  I changed the file permissions to 6755 and it solved the =
problem.

Adriana B.

  ----- Original Message -----=20
  From: Adriana Ballesteros=20
  To: tru64-unix-managers@ornl.gov=20
  Sent: Thursday, August 09, 2001 3:04 PM
