Managers,

I'm running 4.0F on a 433Au workstation. There have been a few summaries =
in the past on how to change the CDE colour depth, which have so far =
failed for me.I have a ZLXp2-EV5 graphics card with the card settings =
set to a resolution of 1024x768 (which is fine for me). The colour depth =
I am achieving is 8 (with a default installation). The card has 2MB =
memory (I think - see below). Essentially I want to improve the screen =
colour display to whatever my card will achieve. Previous summaries =
refer to the Xservers file in /usr/dt/config/Xservers, =
/etc/dt/config/Xservers & /usr/lib/X11/xdm/Xservers and the =
/usr/var/X11/XServer.conf file, specifying options for -depth, =
TrueColor, -vclass etc, none of which seem to increase the colour depth =
(although TrueColour seems to increase the colour depth slightly) after =
a stop/start of the X server (S95 script).=20

Could the problem be that my card is not capable (at this resolution-due =
to memory) of increasing by more than 8-bit ? - I've tried lower res but =
this has no increase in depth.The output from xdypinfo (below) has =
various visual id's - are these the combinations possible with the card =
?

Does anyone have a definitive answer on this (ie which files/options to =
set for cde, output of xdpyinfo, card capabilities), documentation in =
this area seems to be somewhat lacking.

Regards



