Hi, folks.  I'm in Day 4 of  week-long TruCluster Configuration/Management=
 class this week, and my class has come up with some interesting questions=
 that have stumped me.  Hopefull y'all can supply the answers.

Cluster Alias subsystem:

netstat -H or arp -a will tell you who is acting as the router for a=
 cluster alias, so long as you're not on that machine.  But, if you do=
 either command from the member that actually is the alias router at a=
 given time, you won't get back the information.  Is there a command that=
 will tell you which machine is acting as an alias router at a given point=
 in time?

telnet when using cluster aliases:

When you telnet into a cluster alias (default or otherwise), you get back=
 the standard login prompt which includes the hostname for the member.  Is=
 it possible to change this so that the login prompt returns the hostname=
 of the cluster alias used?

telnet question #2:

Say you set up a cluster alias and instruct your users to only telnet=
 through that alias rather than using DEFAULTALIAS.  Is there a way to=
 block port 23 for DEFAULTALIAS while leaving it open for the additonal=
 alias?  Note that we want to do this *inside* Tru64, not outside the o/s,=
 as in on a router.

Fun group this week, good puzzlers.  Hope you guys can provide some=
 insight.  

Cheers,
Ed.
