<DIV><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2>Sorry for the delayed summary, buy my =
servers are=20
ganging up against me.&nbsp; Here is my original post:</FONT></DIV>
<DIV><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2></FONT>&nbsp;</DIV>
<DIV><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2>Ok...it's been a bad week.&nbsp; I have =
yet another=20
question (while still trying to figure out my other problems).&nbsp; =
This has to=20
do with LSM in Tru64 5.1.&nbsp; Our system is a bit odd--let me =
explain.&nbsp;=20
We have a whole bunch of disks on an HSG80 controller--and 4 systems =
connected=20
to the HSG80s (two running 5.0a, one running 4.0f, and the newest one =
runing=20
5.1).&nbsp; The controllers are set to allow ALL hosts to access any of =
the=20
disks.&nbsp; We do not use any clustering at all.&nbsp; These disks =
contain a=20
bunch of Informix databases.&nbsp; We have 6 production images so we use =
LSM to=20
make a group for each image (ie image_01 etc).&nbsp; On any of the =
non-5.1=20
systems I can do whatever I want to the LSM configuration even if =
another system=20
is using the disks at the time--nothing goes wrong as long as two =
systems aren't=20
both trying to write to the disks at the same time.&nbsp; Anyway...I was =
just=20
configuring the new 5.1 system with the LSM, and I enter the=20
following:</FONT></DIV>
<DIV>&nbsp;</DIV>
<DIV><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2>voldisksetup -i dsk12 nlog=3D2 =
nconfig=3D2=20
privlen=3D1024<BR>voldisksetup -i dsk23 nlog=3D2 nconfig=3D2 =
privlen=3D1024</FONT></DIV>
<DIV>&nbsp;</DIV>
<DIV><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2>all of the other systems will be more =
than happy to=20
do this, even if the disks are in use by another system...but the 5.1 =
system=20
says:</FONT></DIV>
<DIV>&nbsp;</DIV>
<DIV><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2>dsk12 is marked in use for LSMpriv in =
the=20
disklabel.<BR>If you continue with the operation you can<BR>possibly =
destroy=20
existing data.<BR>CONTINUE ? [y/n] n</FONT></DIV>
<DIV><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2></FONT>&nbsp;</DIV>
<DIV><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2>So my question is:&nbsp; why doesn't =
this work with=20
a 5.1 system?&nbsp; We do it VERY often with the other systems with no=20
problems.&nbsp; does anyone know of a way around this?&nbsp; I've got a =
call=20
into Compaq, but they hate how we set up our system (even though it =
worked=20
extremely well until now) and always tell us it's not a supported=20
configuration.&nbsp; Anyway...hope this makes some sort of =
sense...</FONT></DIV>
<DIV><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2></FONT>&nbsp;</DIV>
<DIV>########################</DIV>
<DIV>And here is my summary:</DIV>
<DIV>&nbsp;</DIV>
<DIV>After receiving quite a few responses, and a few phone calls with =
compaq,=20
we have somewhat solved our problem.&nbsp; We received that error =
message=20
because LSM had already discovered the disks, and added them to its =
"voldisk=20
list" output.&nbsp; They were online, but not initialized or setup at =
all.&nbsp;=20
So I just had to do a "voldg rm dsk12" for all of the disks.&nbsp; =
</DIV>
<DIV>I am happy I asked this&nbsp;question though, because it turns out =
that LSM=20
in 5.1 is all-new, and the metadata has changed.&nbsp; It is not a =
problem when=20
you move a disk from earlier versions of LSM to the new version (they =
apparently=20
get converted automatically), but being they get converted, you cannot =
put these=20
disks back on a system with an ealier version of LSM.&nbsp; Not too big =
a deal=20
being we will be upgrading all of our servers to 5.1 in the next few=20
weeks.&nbsp; Thanks soo much to all who have replied.&nbsp; </DIV>
<DIV>&nbsp;</DIV>
