X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653669621709

Thanks for the replys. I wasn't clear enough with my question but got
the idea of what I need to do from Alan.

Original Question.
     AS2000, 4.0g, 128MB memory
>
> I am looking for the answer to a question about replacing a complete
> raid set.
> Do I need to remove the AdvFS domain that the raid is mounted on or
just
> replace the drives and rebuild the raid set using the Storage Works
Raid
> Array 200 software?? I am replacing the current 4 4.3GB drives with
new 9.0 GB drives. I don't have space to put the new drives in so I can
do this online so I am doing it on a weekend.

Answers:
alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com wrote:

>         AdvFS can't deal with a device that changes size.  Backup
>         the data, unmount and remove the filesets, remove the
>         domain, reconfigure the subsystem, label the new disk,
>         create a new domain, create and mount new filesets and
>         restore from the backup.
>
>         Alternately, if you have the AdvFS utilities license and
>         can configure a new RAID along side the old one, you can
>         add the new RAID to the existing domain with the addvol
>         command then remove the old RAID with rmvol.  AdvFS will
>         handle migrating the data, and do it online.

Also replied was Pat O'Brien and Tom Webster. both with the same general
jist of the answer.

Now all I am waiting on is for the drives to arrive. Once they get here
I will be ready. Thanks to everyone for your help.



--

Ron Bramblett
Systems Admin
Fuller Brush Company


From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Aug 01 17:03:34 2001
From: "Morris, Matt" <Matt.Morris () avnet ! com>
Date: Wed, 01 Aug 2001 17:03:34 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Summary: KZPAC with 18GB disks
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653669621708

Thanks to all who responded. 


The Original Question:

I understand that there is no support for the 18GB disks under the KZPAC
controller and that Compaq will not support this configuration.
	
That being said, if I group (3) 18GB disks and create (2) RAID 5 StorageSets
(18GB and 16GB Approx.) from them, do you know of any problems (Such as data
loss, redundancy issues, etc...) that I could encounter.  I was under the
impression that 18GB disks couldn't be configured in this manner, but I have
it configured in the Lab now under Tru64 UNIX.  I've labeled the disks,
formatted for UFS and am currently copying data back and forth between the
Luns.

Any input on any possible errors or issues would be appreciated.

Responses:


1) The maximum size supported is 32G and it should be alright.  Again Compaq
does not support 18G in this controller even though it works.


2) The issue is the 32gb logical limit still exists.  Sure you can create a
3-disk (18gb) raid set, but not a logical volume greater than 32gb.


3) We have been running 18G drives on a KZPAC in a raid 5 configuration for
over a year without any problems.  The drives are mounts as UFS partitions
with
oracle data on them.

